I create this code, this stops the animations immediately using a SCRIPT,
StopAnimationById(id);
In id you put the id of the animation you want to stop. I leave it here in case anyone is interested.

@sensen
- simply destroying the sprite does not remove the actual animation sprite instance from MZ's data structures, nor does it inform the animation parent(s) that the animation has ended.
I would recommend something like this instead (untested):
JavaScript:
/*:
 * @target MZ
 * @plugindesc Defines function: StopAnimationById(id)
 * @author Caethyril
 * @url https://forums.rpgmakerweb.com/threads/172519/
 * @help Free to use and/or modify for any project, no credit required.
 */
globalThis.StopAnimationById = function(id) {
  const spriteset = SceneManager._scene._spriteset;
  if (spriteset)
    for (const sprite of spriteset._animationSprites)
      if (sprite._animation.id === id)
        spriteset.removeAnimation(sprite);
};
See
Spriteset_Base#removeAnimation
in rmmz_sprites.js for details.

